{"availability":"available","full":"Sahilll15/shipnotes","name":"shipnotes","description":"Turn a GitHub tag range into grouped release notes where every line links to its PR or commit.","category":"Productivity","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-02T22:35:32Z","updated":"2026-10-08T17:20:42Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://shipnotes-mu.vercel.app","topics":["ai","github-api","nextjs","openai","typescript","vercel"],"demo":"https://shipnotes-mu.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:21:49.281Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:21:49.281Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:21:49.281Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T15:46:30.669Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T18:21:49.281Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Readable release notes from a public GitHub repo and two tags, with every line linked to its PR or commit.","Maintainers need a first draft of a release body, and users want to know what changed between two versions without reading 40 commit messages. ShipNotes reads the commits and merged PRs between two refs, groups them into breaking changes, features, improvements, fixes, docs and internal work, and writes each change as one line. Every line links back to its source, so you can check each one."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Sahilll15/shipnotes/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"eb860c08eae7ff3187a07e08569e497521fa9da8ed1d21a293215a5a2d348811","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T21:29:37.843Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T21:29:37.843Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Readable release notes from a public GitHub repo and two tags, with every line linked to its PR or commit.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Sahilll15/shipnotes/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"eb860c08eae7ff3187a07e08569e497521fa9da8ed1d21a293215a5a2d348811","sourceUrl":"https://github.